text.p:
I Having given 400 Pagodas about two months since to Amid Marcar to buy cloth for me and 4 days since I went to demand my cloth who denied it and said hee stopped my money on account of the last voyage my Ship made who by Contract was to go to Atcheen or Quedah; but the ship falling in with Junckseloan and being in want of wood and water they touched there; and when they were there the Master in two days had got what he wanted and would have proceeded the voyage to Quedah but Amid Marcars Servant entreated him to stay there of which I can produce several witnesses but the Ship staying there and his goods coming to a bad market; hee demands the loss of me which caused our falling out and one of his Servants talking and telling several Impudent Lies I Stroke him being in the Companies Factory on which Amood Marcar went to the avaldar and having feed him with 50 Pagodas I was sent for I being in the Factory denied to go to him till he promised I should return Immediately;
who contrary to his word has Kept me this Three days with a pair of Irons on my Legs and putts me in his peons Cookroom for a Prison and my servants and also Chillimbrum desired ? denied to come to me hee now demanding unjustly 1300 Pagodas for 100 slaves which Amid Marcar has told him went on my Ship without custom paying; which they say I must pay; or else produce the owner of the Slaves; who is Mere Cung Marcar who they all Know very well and that hee now lives at Chiali out of their Reach but they say if I cannot produce him I must pay the money which Justice I referr you to Judge of, this is the Chief thing they demand now; Saying it is the diwans and must bee paid first, but when that is paid they say there is other accounts to make with me for Amood Marcars loss on his goods and Mere Cungs loss on his Slaves; although I have cleared what Mere Cung by Law in Trincumbar having recovered 600 Pagodas of him all which they say I must pay they Intending to ruin me, they having me now in their hands I therefore desire and entreat you would please to order Some person down here and give me your assistance to clear me out of their hands, which unless somebody comes will not bee done by Letters; although the Subidar is willing to release me and has ordered the Avaldar not to let me bee kept in Irons; yett contrary to his order I am and I fear I shall bee still unless assisted by yourself or one of the Councils coming here with the Chief dubash for the Avaldar I am inveterate against me for Chillimbrum speaking for me; and Amid Marcar tells them I am a run away; and no one will Protect me; that they may do what they please with me without fear and therefore as you are my Country men and I hope friends and also by my Protection which I have granted from the Honble. Company I hope and humbly desire your speedy assistance I have not been permitted pen and paper else should have wrote sooner I being treated at the rate of a Murderer they sent Peons on board my Ship yesterday to unhinge her Rudder
but my mate would not permit them which is all at present being not in a Condition of Presenting my Service to you but remain
